% ==============================================================================
% SECTION 8: GENERAL QUIZ
% ==============================================================================
\section{General Quiz: Multiple Choice Strategy}

Multiple choice questions aren't a different kind of maths --- they're the same methods above, with a few test-taking habits that help:

\begin{stepsbox}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
  \item Work out the answer yourself \emph{before} looking at the options, then match it --- don't guess from the options first.
  \item Read every option; the closest-looking wrong answer is often a deliberate trap.
  \item If you're stuck, eliminate options you're sure are wrong, then estimate to pick the most reasonable of what's left.
\end{enumerate}
\end{stepsbox}

\begin{examplebox}{Perimeter of a square, side 7 cm --- options: 14, 28, 49, 21}
Perimeter of a square $=4\times\text{side}=4\times7=\mathbf{28\text{ cm}}$.
\end{examplebox}

\begin{mistakebox}
$49$ is a trap --- that's the \emph{area} ($7\times7$), not the perimeter. Always check you've used the right formula for what's actually being asked.
\end{mistakebox}

